WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.917
Lists are mutable, which means we can change them after they are created.

00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:11.362
We start with twenty-one, nineteen, and twenty-four visits.

00:00:11.362 --> 00:00:13.672
Append adds twenty-seven to the end.

00:00:13.672 --> 00:00:18.347
Then index one is changed from nineteen to twenty.

00:00:18.347 --> 00:00:27.323
Pop zero removes the first value, twenty-one, and also returns it so we can store it in removed_value.

00:00:27.789 --> 00:00:30.781
Run the example one line at a time mentally.

00:00:30.781 --> 00:00:36.226
The final list should contain twenty, twenty-four, and twenty-seven.

00:00:36.226 --> 00:00:41.511
This ability to grow and change is one of the main reasons to use a list.
